{# @block content The trigger, then the panel, in that order. #}
{#
   The ⓘ pattern revealing contextual help, as a native `<details>`: one control
   for mouse, keyboard and touch alike, with no JavaScript.

   Deliberately not a hover. A tooltip revealed on hover alone is unreachable by
   keyboard and slips away from the pointer (WCAG 1.4.13), so the kit's `Tooltip`
   component does not fit here.

   The classes carried are structural: each caller styles its own trigger and
   panel.
#}
<details class="{{ ('relative ' ~ attributes.render('class'))|tailwind_merge }}" {{ attributes.defaults({'data-slot': 'info-disclosure'}) }}>
    {%- block content %}{% endblock -%}
</details>
